From 4c5415b31b92bb5ab9048eec012cf52b886334d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhymabek Roman <robanokssamit@yandex.ru>
Date: Wed, 22 Oct 2026 15:40:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi,dcomp,d3d11,wined3d,server: fix DXGI factory and
 dcomp device creation on software GL hosts

On hosts where wined3d runs on llvmpipe / experimental Intel Xe KMD with
no DRI3 (e.g. Xvfb), DXGI factory creation and the DirectComposition
device path faulted inside dxgi.dll during adapter enumeration and
shared resource setup, killing WinUI 3 apps (WhatsApp Desktop) during
composition device creation.

This completes the staged cross-process surface sharing work:

  * dxgi: adapter/device/swapchain and OpenSharedResource hardening for
    hosts without Vulkan and with a single GL adapter, including NULL
    LUID and cross-process handle plumbing.
  * dcomp: real IDCompositionDevice / desktop device object model with
    composition thread, visual tree compositing, shared visual handles,
    commit completions, CreateSurfaceFromHwnd and partner interfaces.
  * d3d11: device plumbing for the dcomp rendering device.
  * wined3d: GL/Vulkan adapter state fixes for the shared-texture path.
  * server: d3dkmt, token (DISABLE_MAX_PRIVILEGE), named pipe
    (FIRST_PIPE), job limit flags and matching protocol updates.

Tested: CreateDXGIFactory1/EnumAdapters1/EnumAdapterByGpuPreference,
D3D11CreateDevice, DCompositionCreateDevice2, CreateTargetForHwnd,
CreateSurfaceFromHwnd, Commit/WaitForCommitCompletion all S_OK on
Intel Xe + llvmpipe Xvfb; WhatsApp Desktop (WinUI 3) boots past title
bar init with no dxgi fault and stays alive past 60s.

